{"id":4259,"date":"2024-06-25T09:42:43","date_gmt":"2024-06-25T08:42:43","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=4259"},"modified":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","modified_gmt":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","slug":"childrens-ccac-designs-go-on-display-at-the-va-south-kensington","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/childrens-ccac-designs-go-on-display-at-the-va-south-kensington\/","title":{"rendered":"Children\u2019s CCAC designs go on display at the V&amp;A South Kensington"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1400\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-3647 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5.jpg 1920w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5-300x219.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5-1024x747.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5-768x560.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5-1536x1120.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5-274x200.jpg 274w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Copermill5-171x125.jpg 171w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1920px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1920\/1400;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>CCAC\u2019S keenly anticipated display of our pilot programme has opened at the V&amp;A South Kensington.<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The display, which will be in the John Lyon\u2019s Community Gallery, V&amp;A South Kensington until January 2025, includes co-design projects by children from five schools in England. Designers from DaeWha Kang Design, Hassell, Levitt Bernstein Architects, Sylva Studio and Aurelie Fontan pioneered CCAC\u2019s model with 420 schoolchildren.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It was a joy to watch participants in the 2022 pilot programme find their intricate, thoughtful and creative work on the walls of this world-renowned design museum. Children\u2019s enthusiasm and can-do attitude are an inspiration to CCAC and to our partner designers, so it\u2019s always a favourite moment when we see their excitement and pride at public unveilings of their work. And what a place to see one\u2019s work displayed!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">CCAC is hugely proud of all our children and grateful to the expertise and time given by our partner designers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Imagining Tomorrow<\/em> is at the V&amp;A South Kensington until January 2025.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>CCAC\u2019S keenly anticipated display of our pilot programme has opened at the V&#038;A South Kensington<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":4265,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[12],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4259","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-ccac-news"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Children\u2019s CCAC designs go on display at the V&amp;A South Kensington - Climate Change All Change<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/childrens-ccac-designs-go-on-display-at-the-va-south-kensington\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type